@clawsweeper re-review

The identity URL now comes from the active identity ingress. Managed Tailscale Serve uses its lifecycle-owned published hostname; a generic public origin is no longer accepted as proof of Tailscale identity. The same route record serves MCP links, and hello samples it immediately before delivery. Five mismatch/withdrawal regressions failed before the repair; all 52 focused Gateway/lifecycle/MCP tests now pass.

Hosted native testing also exposed asynchronous dashboard recovery ordering and outdated synchronous fixtures. Recovery now retires only its captured older navigation intent when the document changes, while later notifications queue for the successor in the same window. Independent reviews found no actionable P0–P2 findings in either correction. The PR body records exact proof, scope, and the same-task signed-app validation after canonical main deployment.

@clawsweeper re-review

Final head is `5e8273a6f73e00a3ebc605bc8c0fbff0403a7ee4`. The advertised identity URL now comes from the active ingress owner, with mismatch and route-withdrawal regressions passing. Hosted before/after proof also confirms the window-close cancellation repair. The PR body records the signed-app verification after canonical deployment and the production/test LOC split.

The branch was refreshed onto current main to include the existing Browser cleanup repair; all eight task commits remained patch-identical through rebase. The exact original unmocked 14-case Gateway regression now passes with unchanged deadlines. Final exact-head CI is running at https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/33857055937.

@clawsweeper re-review

The final head is ca9133a31ee742e644ec272c3623e46dabcc23b3. The profile fleet lookup now has an explicit await in the canonical connection helper, and the saved-profile reconnect regression uses the production default identity resolver. Exact a033 Mac Release and all 2,096 app tests passed, so the reported old-head compile failure was not reproduced.

Independent review found an additional lifecycle gap: already-open saved-profile windows did not observe new hello identity announcements. The final repair subscribes per open profile, uses per-profile revision/pending state to isolate disconnects, and preserves later native-window selections and commands. Frozen before-proof 33863729386 failed only the intended reconnect test (six assertions for changed/withdrawn URLs); final compile and scoped review pass. Exact final CI 33865765617 and whole-PR integration review are running. The PR body contains the proof and remaining deployment-stage SSO verification.
